l back on, resulting in the \"Check device power\" message.\n\n\nThe kernel decompression failure stems from the incorrect load address set by `env_unlocked.img`. This causes corruption during the decompression process, leading to the aborted `bootm` command. Consequently, U-Boot enters `DNL mode [TPL]` with the HDMI signal disabled, resulting in the observed symptoms: a solid green LED and the \"Check device power\" message on the TV.\n\nThis USB-based `DNL mode` can likely fix the box quickly.\n\n\nThe USB-based `DNL mode` provides a viable recovery path. Applying the `adnl.exe` commands will: (1) set the correct `loadaddr` in the environment; (2) flash the updated environment; (3) flash the genuine recovery image; and (4) reboot the device. On reboot, the correct `loadaddr` ensures kernel decompression occurs at the expected memory location. This prevents corruption, enabling the successful boot of Android 12 and HDMI activation.\n\n\nThe updated logic focuses on immediate USB detection of the `DNL mode [TPL]` device (`VID_1B8E&PID_C004`). When detected, it will run a set of commands to: (1) set the correct load address, (2) flash the updated environment, (3) flash the recovery image, and (4) reboot the device to ensure successful boot into Android 12. This approach leverages the identified USB connection to correct the boot process.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\andre\\\\OneDrive\\\\Desktop\\\\xview\\\\programa perfecto\\\\1_HERRAMIENTAS_MOTOR\\\\ProgramaPerfecto.cs\"","Replacement":"\"        static ToolResult InvokeFastbootSafe(string argString, int timeoutMs = 3000, bool logCmd = true)\\n        {\\n            return InvokeToolSafe(FASTBOOT_EXE, argString, timeoutMs, logCmd);\\n        }\\n\\n        static ToolResult InvokeAdnlSafe(string argString, int timeoutMs = 2500, bool logCmd = true)\\n        {\\n            return InvokeToolSafe(ADNL_EXE, argString, timeoutMs, logCmd);\\n        }\\n\\n        static Tool